Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:23:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/23] sheet route: memory budget coefficient from the
 measured Schur peak

Sixty production labels through the budgeted queue put the peak RSS of
the Schur stage at 33 MB per 1000 fine Tet10 dof; the reservation was
45 MB and held about 35 percent of the budget idle.  Now 36 MB, a ten
percent margin.  Thread count per job made no difference to the Schur
time per unit work (104 vs 105 s per 100k tetrahedra at 8 and 12
threads): the queue is bound by the memory budget, not by threads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X77H1Uihff2oEyM5T4qg7v
